      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand you're worried and want to help your child, but giving your child aspirin at home is not advised, especially because he's under 16 years old and has a fever. Aspirin can cause a serious condition called Reye's syndrome in children, particularly when they have a virus or flu-like symptoms. It's crucial to contact your pediatrician for guidance or seek immediate medical attention if you think your child’s condition is severe. Don’t give aspirin and let your pediatrician know as soon as possible.",
